Upstream: https://www.sqlite.org/
License: blessing (SQLite, a public-domain dedication); BSD-2-Clause (linenoise); MIT (musl, Zig runtime)
Built from source by BundleDock because sqlite.org publishes no linux-arm64 command-line
build. The recipe is the sqlite3 entry of packages.catalog.json.

SQLite source: the amalgamation ZIP named by the lock (first pinned release 3.54.1,
https://www.sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3540100.zip). The lock records the
SHA3-256 taken from the product data of https://www.sqlite.org/download.html and the
SHA256 of the same bytes; the builder verifies both before it unpacks the file.

linenoise source: https://github.com/antirez/linenoise, pinned by commit
a473823d74b93eab2ba83480df16ed37617493f2 (files linenoise.c, linenoise.h and LICENSE,
fetched from raw.githubusercontent.com at that commit). The upstream publishes no
checksum, so the lock records the builder-computed SHA256 of each file (verification
class tls-download-sha256, the named exception of AGENTS.md); a bump of this commit
needs the owner's approval.

Toolchain: zig 0.17.0 (https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.0/), pinned in the lock by the
SHA256 listed for each architecture in https://ziglang.org/download/index.json. The musl
and Zig license files in this directory are those of that archive (lib/libc/musl/COPYRIGHT
and LICENSE; the two architectures' archives carry identical musl COPYRIGHT bytes).
The compiler runs only at build time, without network access.

The SQLite blessing in NOTICE was read from the header of sqlite3.h in the verified
amalgamation. No upstream executable was run; the output is checked for static linking
by the builder.
